                <main class="aisa-main">
                    <form id="aisa-settings" action="<?php echo esc_url(admin_url('admin-post.php')); ?>" method="post" hidden><input type="hidden" name="action" value="aisa_save"><?php wp_nonce_field('aisa_admin'); ?></form>
                    <section id="aisa-overview" class="aisa-section">
                        <div class="aisa-hero"><p class="aisa-eyebrow">OVERVIEW</p><h1>Helpful support.<br>Your rules.</h1><p>Choose a model, approve what it knows, and make the experience yours.</p><div class="aisa-hero-tags"><?php self::badge($s['enabled']?'Chat enabled · untested':'Chat disabled',$s['enabled']?'warning':'muted'); self::badge('Runtime verification pending','warning'); ?></div></div>
                        <div class="aisa-metrics"><div><span>PROVIDER</span><strong><?php echo esc_html($providerNames[$s['provider']]??'Unknown provider'); ?></strong><small><?php echo esc_html($provider); ?></small></div><div><span>KNOWLEDGE SOURCES</span><strong><?php echo esc_html($sources); ?></strong><small>Stored sources · approval checked per record</small></div><div><span>LEARNING QUEUE</span><strong><?php echo esc_html($suggestions); ?></strong><small>Suggestions waiting for your review</small></div></div>
                        <div class="aisa-card"><h2>A deliberate start</h2><ol class="aisa-checklist"><li><a href="#aisa-providers">Choose your provider and exact model ID</a><span>Saved settings do not prove a successful connection.</span></li><li><a href="#aisa-knowledge">Review and approve your support sources</a><span>Imported, indexed and changed content waits for approval.</span></li><li><a href="#aisa-notifications">Add a human support destination</a><span>Give customers a way to continue with your team.</span></li><li><a href="#aisa-diagnostics">Complete staging verification</a><span>Test permissions, downloads, failures and theme behavior.</span></li></ol><div class="aisa-divider"></div><?php $field('enabled','Enable customer chat','checkbox'); ?><p class="aisa-help">Off by default. Enabling this can send customer questions and approved public facts to the selected model provider. Review your privacy notice and provider terms first.</p></div>
                    </section>
                    <section id="aisa-providers" class="aisa-section">
                        <?php self::heading('02','Providers','Your choice of model. Server-side credentials.'); ?>
                        <div class="aisa-card"><div class="aisa-card-top"><h3>Model connection</h3><?php self::badge($provider,'warning'); ?></div>
                            <div class="aisa-field-grid"><label class="aisa-field"><span>Provider</span><select form="aisa-settings" name="provider"><?php foreach (array('openai'=>'OpenAI','gemini'=>'Google Gemini','nvidia'=>'NVIDIA','groq'=>'Groq','compatible'=>'OpenAI-compatible API','local'=>'Local / self-hosted gateway') as $key=>$label) { ?><option value="<?php echo esc_attr($key); ?>" <?php selected($s['provider'],$key); ?>><?php echo esc_html($label); ?></option><?php } ?></select></label><?php $field('model','Exact model ID'); $field('secret','Model API key','password'); $field('endpoint','Custom chat completions URL','url'); ?></div>
                            <p class="aisa-help">Custom URL is used only for compatible and local providers. Use an authenticated public HTTPS gateway for local inference; direct localhost/LAN access is blocked by safe HTTP. Verify model availability and gateway authentication separately. No provider calls run when this panel opens or saves. Incomplete, refused, tool-call and malformed answers fall back to human support. Model calls are never retried automatically.</p>
                            <div class="aisa-divider"></div><h3>Usage boundaries</h3><div class="aisa-field-grid"><?php $field('daily_limit','Model requests per site / day','number'); $field('hourly_limit','Requests per visitor / hour','number'); ?></div><p class="aisa-help">Requests and output tokens are bounded. This is not a currency budget; set spending limits with your provider too. Free tiers and quotas may change.</p>
                        </div>
                    </section>
                    <section id="aisa-widget" class="aisa-section">
                        <?php self::heading('03','Widget','Small details that make support feel like your site.'); ?>
                        <div class="aisa-card"><h3>Bounded public context memory</h3><?php $field('memory','Allow visitors to opt in to context memory','checkbox'); ?><p class="aisa-help">Off by default, with a separate visitor opt-in in each tab. Stores approved public source/product IDs and approval fingerprints only, never questions, replies, credentials, orders or download links. Histories are separate per site, account, login session and widget session. Maximum 4 turns, 15 minutes absolute expiry, 8 KB state and 2,048 byte-per-token budget units for recalled facts (not an exact provider tokenizer). Each turn rechecks approval and source freshness. Clear chat resets context; disabling this setting invalidates all prior scopes. This supports public-topic follow-ups, not verbatim transcript recall.</p></div>
                        <div class="aisa-two-column"><div class="aisa-card"><h3>Brand & appearance</h3><?php $field('title','Chat heading'); $field('welcome','Welcome message'); ?><div class="aisa-field-grid"><?php $field('color','Accent color','color'); $field('radius','Corner radius (0–32)','number'); ?></div><label class="aisa-field"><span>Placement</span><select form="aisa-settings" name="position"><option value="right" <?php selected($s['position'],'right'); ?>>Right</option><option value="left" <?php selected($s['position'],'left'); ?>>Left</option></select></label><p class="aisa-help">The preview shows saved values. Save to refresh it. Widget styles are isolated from your theme; verify mobile, focus and contrast on staging.</p></div>
                            <div class="aisa-preview-stage"><span class="aisa-preview-caption">SAVED APPEARANCE · <?php echo esc_html(strtoupper($s['position'])); ?></span><div class="aisa-widget-preview" style="--aisa-preview-accent:<?php echo esc_attr(sanitize_hex_color($s['color'])?:'#635bff'); ?>;--aisa-preview-radius:<?php echo (int)max(0,min(32,$s['radius'])); ?>px" aria-label="Saved widget appearance preview"><div class="aisa-preview-header"><span aria-hidden="true">✦</span><strong><?php echo esc_html($s['title']); ?><small>AI assistant · Support options</small></strong></div><div class="aisa-preview-messages"><p><?php echo esc_html($s['welcome']); ?></p><span class="aisa-preview-chip">My purchases</span><span class="aisa-preview-chip">Talk to a person</span></div><div class="aisa-preview-composer"><span>How can we help?</span><span class="aisa-preview-send">Send</span></div><small class="aisa-preview-footer">Appearance preview · no messages sent</small></div></div>
                        </div>
                    </section>
                    <section id="aisa-knowledge" class="aisa-section">
                        <?php self::heading('04','Knowledge approvals','Only the version you review can become an answer.'); ?>
                        <div class="aisa-card"><h3>Instructions & review policy</h3><?php $field('instructions','Administrator instructions','textarea'); $field('learning','Allow customer suggestions for review','checkbox'); ?><p class="aisa-help">Saving administrator instructions makes them active configuration. Sources and suggestions require separate approval below. Conversations are not stored or used to train model weights. Never add secrets or private customer details as knowledge.</p></div>
                        <div class="aisa-two-column"><div class="aisa-card"><h3>Index your public site</h3><p>Public posts, pages and visible products are collected in batches of 50. Collection never means approval.</p><form method="post" action="<?php echo esc_url(admin_url('admin-post.php')); ?>"><input type="hidden" name="action" value="aisa_index"><?php wp_nonce_field('aisa_admin'); ?><button class="button" type="submit">Index next batch</button></form><p class="aisa-help">Initial collection uses WP-Cron. Use manual batches when scheduled events are disabled or have no traffic. Re-index older sources before reviewing them.</p></div><div class="aisa-card"><h3>Import a support document</h3><p>UTF-8 TXT or Markdown, up to 256 KB. Imports stay unavailable until approved.</p><form method="post" enctype="multipart/form-data" action="<?php echo esc_url(admin_url('admin-post.php')); ?>"><input type="hidden" name="action" value="aisa_upload"><?php wp_nonce_field('aisa_admin'); ?><label class="aisa-upload">Public support file<input required type="file" name="knowledge" accept=".txt,.md"></label><button class="button" type="submit">Import for review</button></form></div></div>
                        <div class="aisa-card aisa-source-list"><div class="aisa-card-top"><h3>Customer suggestions</h3><?php self::badge($suggestions.' pending'); ?></div><?php $drafts=get_posts(array('post_type'=>'aisa_draft','post_status'=>'pending','posts_per_page'=>20)); foreach ($drafts as $draft) { $review($draft); } if (!$drafts) { ?><p class="aisa-empty">No suggestions waiting. Customer conversations are not stored.</p><?php } ?></div>
                        <div class="aisa-card aisa-source-list"><h3>Source review</h3><p class="aisa-help">Approval covers the full text shown and its source snapshot. Changed content, product facts or revoked approval cannot be used by chat or either MCP search tool. Existing sources are retained; they are not auto-approved.</p>
                            <?php $page=max(1,absint($_GET['knowledge_page']??1)); $query=new WP_Query(array('post_type'=>'aisa_knowledge','post_status'=>'private','posts_per_page'=>20,'paged'=>$page,'orderby'=>'ID','order'=>'ASC')); foreach ($query->posts as $source) { $review($source); } if (!$query->posts) { ?><p class="aisa-empty">No sources on this page. Index your site or import a support file to begin.</p><?php } ?>
                            <nav class="aisa-pagination" aria-label="Knowledge source pages"><?php if ($page>1) { ?><a class="button" href="<?php echo esc_url(add_query_arg(array('page'=>'aisa','knowledge_page'=>$page-1),admin_url('admin.php')).'#aisa-knowledge'); ?>">Previous sources</a><?php } ?><span>Page <?php echo esc_html($page); ?> of <?php echo esc_html(max(1,$query->max_num_pages)); ?></span><?php if ($page<$query->max_num_pages) { ?><a class="button" href="<?php echo esc_url(add_query_arg(array('page'=>'aisa','knowledge_page'=>$page+1),admin_url('admin.php')).'#aisa-knowledge'); ?>">Next sources</a><?php } ?></nav>
                        </div>
                    </section>
                    <section id="aisa-woocommerce" class="aisa-section">
                        <?php self::heading('05','WooCommerce','Private purchases stay behind the customer account.'); ?>
                        <?php if ($woocommerce && get_option('woocommerce_downloads_require_login','no')!=='yes') { ?><div class="aisa-callout">Download login requirement is off in WooCommerce. Its native file links can act as bearer links even though this widget only reveals them to the owning account. Enable Downloads require login in WooCommerce download settings if file access must also require the signed-in owner. This plugin does not change that store setting.</div><?php } ?>
                        <div class="aisa-card"><div class="aisa-card-top"><h3>Account access & downloads</h3><?php self::badge($woocommerce?'Detected · untested':'Not detected',$woocommerce?'warning':'muted'); ?></div><p><?php echo $woocommerce?'WooCommerce functions are available. That does not verify your store’s ownership or download behavior.':'WooCommerce is optional. Product, order and download features need WooCommerce; this panel does not install it.'; ?></p><ul class="aisa-feature-list"><li>Customers sign in to see their own purchases.</li><li>Download links come from WooCommerce’s available-download permissions.</li><li>Guest purchases need human assistance or account linking.</li><li>Payment claims in chat cannot mark an order paid, refund it or delete data.</li></ul><div class="aisa-callout">Before public use, test two separate accounts plus pending, paid, refunded, expired and revoked downloads. No order details are sent to the model.</div><div class="aisa-divider"></div><h3>Public payment guidance</h3><?php $field('payment_text','Public payment instructions','textarea'); $field('qr_url','Public payment QR image URL','url'); ?><p class="aisa-help">These values appear in customer chat. Never include private payment credentials. QR images and chat claims are not payment confirmation. Product catalog facts need approval; price, stock and other changes may require re-indexing and re-approval.</p></div>
                    </section>
                    <section id="aisa-notifications" class="aisa-section">
                        <?php self::heading('06','Notifications / Handoff','Give your team a clear way to take over.'); ?>
                        <div class="aisa-card"><div class="aisa-card-top"><h3>Human support</h3><?php self::badge($handoff?'Contact set · untested':'Contact missing',$handoff?'muted':'warning'); ?></div><div class="aisa-field-grid"><?php $field('support_email','Customer support email','email'); $field('handoff_url','Human support / WhatsApp URL','url'); ?></div><p class="aisa-help">The widget offers these contact links and requests an admin notification. It does not submit a local review ticket or guarantee a reply. WhatsApp uses your link or a separately configured relay.</p></div>
                        <?php AISA_Inbox::render(); ?>
                        <div class="aisa-card"><?php $field('customer_tickets','Enable account-linked structured handoff tickets','checkbox'); ?><p class="aisa-help">Off by default. Review identity, consent, retention and theme behavior on disposable staging before enabling elsewhere. The signed-in widget offers explicit topic-only submission and own-ticket status. No transcript capture, notification, reply or refund. The widget is available when customer chat is enabled; ticket submission does not call the model.</p></div>
                        <?php AISA_Handoff::render(); ?>
                        <div class="aisa-card"><h3>Admin event notifications</h3><div class="aisa-channel-status"><div><strong>Email</strong><?php self::badge($email?'Configured · untested':'Not configured'); ?></div><div><strong>Telegram</strong><?php self::badge($telegram?'Configured · untested':'Incomplete'); ?></div><div><strong>HTTPS relay</strong><?php self::badge($relay?'Configured · untested':'Not configured'); ?></div></div><div class="aisa-field-grid"><?php $field('notify_email','Admin notification email','email'); $field('telegram_secret','Telegram bot token','password'); $field('telegram_chat','Telegram chat ID'); $field('webhook_secret','HTTPS relay URL','password'); ?></div><p class="aisa-help">Events: paid purchase and human support request. Payloads contain event type and site name; purchase events include order ID. Message text and customer contact details are omitted. Saving sends no test notification.</p><div class="aisa-callout">Delivery is synchronous and has no retry queue. Ambiguous failures are not automatically resent because destinations may duplicate alerts. Verify your gateway’s payment-complete hook and each destination with disposable test data before relying on alerts.</div></div>
                    </section>
                    <section id="aisa-mcp" class="aisa-section">
                        <?php self::heading('07','MCP','A narrow, read-only connection to approved public facts.'); ?>
                        <div class="aisa-card"><div class="aisa-card-top"><h3>Inbound MCP server</h3><?php self::badge(!$s['mcp']?'Disabled':(!is_ssl()?'Blocked on HTTP':'Enabled · untested'),$s['mcp']?'warning':'muted'); ?></div><?php $field('mcp','Enable authenticated read-only MCP','checkbox'); ?><div class="aisa-endpoint"><span>ENDPOINT</span><code><?php echo esc_html(rest_url('aisa/v1/mcp')); ?></code></div><p>Available tools: <code>search_catalog</code> and <code>search_knowledge</code>. Both require approved content. Private orders, downloads, refunds and arbitrary remote actions are not exposed.</p><p class="aisa-help">Connect over HTTPS using a dedicated WordPress administrator Application Password. Create/manage it separately; this plugin does not generate credentials. Limited protocol profile: 2025-06-18 JSON-RPC over stateless POST. Supports initialize, notifications, ping, tools/list and tools/call. Full Streamable HTTP transport and client interoperability are unverified; use a compatible custom transport and verify your client separately. Outbound MCP connections are not implemented.</p></div>
                    </section>
                    <section id="aisa-diagnostics" class="aisa-section">
                        <?php self::heading('08','Diagnostics','Observed configuration, with honest limits.'); ?>
                        <div class="aisa-card"><h3>Environment snapshot</h3><dl class="aisa-diagnostics"><div><dt>Plugin / PHP</dt><dd><?php echo esc_html(AISA_VERSION.' / '.PHP_VERSION); ?></dd></div><div><dt>WordPress</dt><dd><?php echo esc_html(get_bloginfo('version')); ?></dd></div><div><dt>HTTPS request</dt><dd><?php self::badge(is_ssl()?'Detected':'Not detected',is_ssl()?'muted':'warning'); ?></dd></div><div><dt>Credential encryption</dt><dd><?php self::badge(function_exists('openssl_encrypt') && function_exists('openssl_decrypt')?'OpenSSL available':'OpenSSL missing','warning'); ?></dd></div><div><dt>Model credential</dt><dd><?php self::badge($credentials['model']?'Stored and decryptable · untested':'Missing or unreadable','warning'); ?></dd></div><div><dt>Scheduled indexing</dt><dd><?php echo defined('DISABLE_WP_CRON') && DISABLE_WP_CRON?'WP-Cron disabled · use manual batches':'WP-Cron not disabled in configuration · execution unverified'; ?></dd></div><div><dt>Runtime verification</dt><dd><?php self::badge('Untested on this site','warning'); ?></dd></div></dl><p class="aisa-help">This panel reads local settings and available functions. It does not certify provider connectivity, delivery, order permissions or theme compatibility. Salt changes can make saved credentials unreadable; re-enter them after rotation.</p><details class="aisa-verification"><summary>What to verify on disposable staging</summary><ul class="aisa-feature-list"><li>Provider success, timeout, quota and invalid-response behavior.</li><li>Two-account order isolation, guest/expired login rejection and download expiry/revocation.</li><li>Admin permissions, REST cookie nonces, MCP Application Password authentication and HTTPS.</li><li>Approval after source changes; product pricing, tax/location and translated URLs.</li><li>Notification delivery with disposable destinations; keyboard, mobile, theme CSS and multisite isolation.</li></ul></details></div>
                        <div class="aisa-card"><div class="aisa-card-top"><h3>Recent audit events</h3><span class="aisa-help">Latest 15 · rolling retention</span></div><ol class="aisa-audit"><?php $events=get_posts(array('post_type'=>'aisa_audit','post_status'=>'private','posts_per_page'=>15)); foreach ($events as $event) { ?><li><time><?php echo esc_html($event->post_date); ?></time><span><?php echo esc_html($event->post_title); ?></span></li><?php } ?></ol><?php if (!$events) { ?><p class="aisa-empty">No recorded events yet. This is not proof that connections work.</p><?php } ?><p class="aisa-help">Audit events omit raw conversations, provider responses and keys. An event records an attempt; it is not a delivery receipt.</p></div>
